  "question": {
    "text": "Gaseous cyclobutene isomerizes to butadiene in a first order process which has a &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&#39; value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>153</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The time in minutes it takes for the isomerization to proceed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>%</mo></math>&nbsp;to completion at this temperature is_____. (Rounded off to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
